  "answer": "A **council vote** involves a panel of independent evaluators who each cast a simultaneous ballot; the option with majority (or plurality) support wins. It uniquely differs by relying on parallel democratic tallying rather than sequential contests or any blending of content.\n\nA tournament pick chooses one winner via successive pairwise contests or elimination brackets. It uniquely differs by using competitive sequential matchups rather than a council vote’s simultaneous majority tally or a fusion merge’s blending of all inputs into one hybrid.\n\nA **fusion merge** integrates the best elements, insights, or data from multiple sources into a single hybrid result. It uniquely differs by synthesizing contributions rather than selecting one winner via vote or contest.",
